# Cloud Deployment Instructions

## AWS EC2 Deployment

# 1. Launch an EC2 instance
# - Use Ubuntu Server 22.04 LTS
# - t2.micro (free tier)
# - Security group: allow inbound TCP ports 22 (SSH), 80 (HTTP), 8000 (API)

# 2. SSH into the instance
chmod 400 your-key.pem
ssh -i "your-key.pem" ubuntu@<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>

# 3. Install Docker
sudo apt update
sudo apt install docker.io -y
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
newgrp docker

# 4. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/your-username/audio-api.git
cd audio-api

# 5. Build and run the Docker container
docker build -t audio-api .
docker run -d -p 80:8000 audio-api

# 6. Test remotely
# - Swagger UI: http://<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>/docs
# - Postman:
#   - Method: POST
#   - URL: http://<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>/predict-audio/
#   - Body: form-data → key='file', type='File', upload .wav/.mp3 file

## GCP Cloud Run Deployment

# 1. Install the gcloud CLI
curl https://sdk.cloud.google.com | bash
exec -l $SHELL
gcloud init

# 2. Build and push the Docker image
gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/your-project-id/audio-api

# 3. Deploy to Cloud Run
gcloud run deploy audio-api \
  --image gcr.io/your-project-id/audio-api \
  --platform managed \
  --region us-central1 \
  --allow-unauthenticated \
  --port 8000

# 4. Test remotely
# - Get the service URL from the deploy output
# - Swagger UI: https://<SERVICE_URL>/docs
# - Postman:
#   - Method: POST
#   - URL: https://<SERVICE_URL>/predict-audio/
#   - Body: form-data → key='file', type='File', upload .wav/.mp3 file
